          "So a relational approach separates three things. Preferences (food, music, hobbies, style) can be flexed generously and often. Values and convictions (honesty, faith, ethics) are held firmly but kindly (Rom 14:23). Needs and safety (rest, health, freedom from harm) are not traded away. Changing an interest because you have come to enjoy it, or freely choosing to join in for love, is beautiful. Pretending, or being pressured to give up who you are, is not."
